content.summary_of_the_paper:
This paper combines three objective functions for the self-supervised visual pre-training on ImageNet.

(1) The alignment between the two different views of an identical image, which is very common for existing methods;

(2) The covariance term to bring the off-diagonal coefficients of the features' covariance matrix to zero, which is modified from the Barlow Twins;

(3) The variance term that defines a hinge function on the standard deviation of embeddings along the batch dimension for every specific dimension of the feature projections . To the best of the reviewer's knowledge, such objective function is firstly applied for the visual pre-training in this paper, although the same measure has been used to analyze the model collapse problem (e.g., in the paper of SimSiam), but not be designed as a specific pre-trained loss function.
